WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:01.403
- It's hot.

00:00:01.403 --> 00:00:02.726
- [Katie] Do you like hot food?

00:00:02.726 --> 00:00:03.559
- No.

00:00:03.559 --> 00:00:04.392
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:04.392 --> 00:00:06.975
(upbeat music)

00:00:14.127 --> 00:00:16.830
- Hi, I'm Kelly, I'm a culinary
producer here at Tasty.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:17.700
- Hi, I'm Jeremy.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.470
I'm a chef and Kelly's husband

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:22.020
and we have two boys
together, Dylan and Teddy.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:24.270
- And we are about to
have our third this fall.

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:25.830
Yay!
(Kelly applauding)

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.200
- So last time we were
here, Tasty challenged us

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.930
to see who could make the
best lunch for our son, Dylan,

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:33.870
and I won and I've had the
bragging rights ever since.

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:36.570
- But today, I finally get
the chance to redeem myself

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:38.250
because Tasty invited us back

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.650
to see who could make the
best breakfast for Dylan.

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:42.390
- [Katie] Do you guys wanna
add some stakes to this?

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:43.920
- I think whoever wins gets

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:45.750
to choose the next family adventure.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:49.260
I wanna go to a really
nice hotel with a pool.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:51.298
- And I want to go to a punk rock concert.

00:00:51.298 --> 00:00:52.680
- Oh, my God.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:54.270
Yeah, that's our personalities.

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:55.320
All right, let's do it.
(Kelly and Jeremy high-fiving)

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:56.908
May the best man win.

00:00:56.908 --> 00:00:57.741
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:57.741 --> 00:00:59.610
Today, I'm making a beach
themed breakfast for Dylan.

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:00.720
He is a water baby.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:01.590
He is a water sign.

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:03.060
He's always loved the beach

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:04.410
and I think he's really gonna love this.

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:06.930
So the first thing I'm
gonna make is some pancakes

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:08.820
and I'm gonna shape them into a sailboat.

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:10.950
So we have some, any milk we'll do.

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:12.090
This is almond milk.

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:13.020
That's vanilla.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:15.270
A little maple syrup because you need it.

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:19.290
And then bananas, some oats,
and then some baking powder.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:21.480
And of course, a little
salt and some eggs.

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:24.300
I love these pancakes
because it requires no whisk,

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:25.800
you can just put
everything in the blender.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:26.790
It's whole ingredients.

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:29.170
It's super healthy and the kids love them.

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:30.863
(blender whirring)

00:01:30.863 --> 00:01:31.696
- So this looks good.

00:01:31.696 --> 00:01:34.020
And for easy pouring,
I'm just gonna put it

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:36.480
in a squeeze bottle just
so I can pour it easier

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:37.313
into the pan.

00:01:37.313 --> 00:01:38.520
So I have a pan heating.

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:39.720
I'm just gonna add some butter

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:41.700
because you can't make a
pancake without butter.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:44.220
Dylan loves pancakes, but to be honest,

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:46.590
I don't think I'm gonna
beat Jeremy this time.

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:47.880
I make the boys lunch every day,

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:49.800
but Jeremy really does the
breakfast in our house,

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:51.720
so we'll see.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:53.820
So I'm gonna try to
make a pancake sailboat.

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:56.760
So I'm gonna make a half
circle to do the bottom.

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:57.593
It's cute.

00:01:57.593 --> 00:01:58.710
I'm gonna fill it in.

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:00.690
I've never done pancake art before,

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:03.852
but I've seen it on TikTok,
so that's like college.

00:02:03.852 --> 00:02:04.685
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:04.685 --> 00:02:06.690
It's bubbling up top,
so I'm gonna flip it.

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:07.523
Hopefully, it looks good.

00:02:07.523 --> 00:02:09.030
Hey, that's not bad.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:10.290
So I'm also gonna cook
it on the other side,

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:12.060
probably like 30 to 60 seconds.

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:14.250
My little boat is done,
I'm gonna take it out.

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:16.560
And then I'm gonna clean
this out and make the sails.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:19.710
Dylan's not really a picky
eater, he'll eat a lot of food.

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:21.330
He's outgrown that picky eater stage.

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:22.710
Our other son is in it right now.

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:24.240
We're just gonna let
these cook probably one

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:25.500
to two minutes until they're bubbling

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:26.430
and then flip 'em over.

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:27.860
My little triangles are done.

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:31.530
It's not as cute as I had
up here, but you know what?

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:32.370
As long as it tastes good.

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:35.250
So the next thing I'm gonna be
making is sand for the beach.

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:37.200
And I'm actually gonna use
scrambled eggs for that.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.450
Crack some eggs and then a little salt.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:40.560
Jeremy always makes fun of me

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.300
that this is the most annoying sound.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:44.640
He's always like, "I think
you're done beating them."

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:47.550
I think the secret to really
good scrambled eggs is,

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:49.890
obviously, butter and low and slow.

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:51.300
I'm just gonna pour these in here.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:53.700
Some people will constantly be stirring it

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:55.740
and that will get you really small curds.

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:59.160
But I actually like them to
kind of be bigger, softer,

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:00.180
like clouds.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.290
These are looking perfect.

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:03.450
I'm gonna take them off the
heat so they stop cooking

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:04.530
and let's go to the next step.

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:09.000
So the next thing I'm making
is avocado toast palm tree.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.790
I've never done this before,
but I need to take some bread

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:13.830
and cut it into the palm leaves,

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:16.020
and then toast it so I
can put avocado on top.

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:17.700
I hope this works.

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:19.530
I think I have to do the crust

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:21.720
to make it keep it shape, which is fine.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:25.170
Dylan actually likes
crust, so no problem there.

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:28.110
Once I put the avocado on it
and it'll look like a leaf,

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:28.943
this is working.

00:03:28.943 --> 00:03:29.871
Just stay with me, guys.

00:03:29.871 --> 00:03:31.055
Just stay with me.
(Kelly laughing)

00:03:31.055 --> 00:03:32.940
I'm just gonna pop these
in a 400 degree oven

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:36.150
for five to six minutes, just
until they're lightly toasted.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:37.890
My toast is toasted.

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:40.740
Now I have to cut an
avocado to perfectly fit

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:43.830
on top of that bread
to make little leaves.

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:45.180
I'm just gonna cut it in half.

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:48.510
So I cut the avocado in
half and then in quarters.

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:50.070
And then I'm just gonna cut little slivers

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:51.420
to make the palm leaves.

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:53.430
But first, let me actually
put some lemon on it

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:54.263
so it doesn't brown.

00:03:54.263 --> 00:03:55.920
So I'm gonna try to trim the toast

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:57.390
to the shape of the avocado.

00:03:57.390 --> 00:04:01.170
And then I'm gonna cut some
little slits like this,

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:03.000
give it the palm leaf look.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:05.640
Let me just season it with
some salt and then look.

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:07.140
So I'm gonna repeat this with the rest

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:09.180
of my toast and then
move on to the next step.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:11.310
Now that most of my elements are done,

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:12.930
I'm gonna work on the final touches,

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:16.170
which is creating sea
creatures out of tons of fruit.

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:17.640
This big boy is a cantaloupe

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:20.220
which Dylan just started liking.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:21.450
So for this one,

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:23.850
I found this cute little
fish cookie cutter

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:26.070
and I'm gonna cut out
some fish from cantaloupe.

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:27.570
Okay, this one worked.

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:29.040
Look at the little fishy.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:31.740
And then I'm gonna make
a dragon fruit starfish.

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:34.980
Now, I don't think Dylan's
ever had this, to be honest.

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:37.860
I'm gonna use this starfish cookie cutter

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:38.850
to make some starfish.

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:40.710
Look how cute it is.

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:42.900
Things like these would drive Jeremy nuts.

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:44.970
He doesn't have the
patience to cut things out

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:45.960
of little shapes.

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:47.310
Maybe that's why I'm gonna win.

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:49.530
The next thing I'm gonna do is try

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:51.810
to make a turtle out of a kiwi.

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:54.090
So this will be our little body.

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:56.460
And then I gotta cut a head and some legs.

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:57.900
Here's our little head.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:00.060
Ready to cut the little
feet so I made a circle

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:02.460
and then I'm just gonna
cut the circle in half

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:03.750
and make its little leg.

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:05.160
There he has four little legs.

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:05.993
Does it look like it?

00:05:05.993 --> 00:05:08.880
Just to give our little
turtle friend some eyes,

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:09.870
mini chocolate chips.

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:11.040
I think he's cute.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.230
Now I'm gonna make a
little strawberry crab.

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:15.420
I just cut another round for its body.

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:18.180
I'm just cutting little rectangles.

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:20.760
And then the little antennas here.

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:22.650
This is definitely not what I envisioned,

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:23.880
but we have to go with it.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:26.430
And I'll just add some
chocolate chips for eyes

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:28.200
and, hopefully, Dylan will love it.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:29.760
I think he's actually pretty cute,

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:32.400
so let's make our final
thing, which is a sun

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:36.600
which I'm gonna do is slice
an orange, and for the rays,

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:39.240
I'm just gonna do some dried apricots.

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:42.780
Dylan actually loves dried
apricots, any dried fruit really.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:45.120
The last thing we have to do
is assemble it all together.

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:47.310
I'm actually so excited to assemble this.

00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:50.520
I'm gonna do half savory and half sweet,

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:51.900
so we get a little bit of both.

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:54.630
For the savory side, we're
gonna do some of our eggs

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:56.250
as the sand.

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:57.780
And then for the palm tree,

00:05:57.780 --> 00:06:01.163
I actually cooked up some maple
sausage and I'm gonna make

00:06:01.163 --> 00:06:05.130
that to the trunk by just
stacking a few up top.

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:08.790
And then we have our avocado
toast for our palm leaves.

00:06:08.790 --> 00:06:11.370
For little coconuts, we're
gonna do some blueberries,

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:12.930
which Dylan also loves.

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:14.910
For the ocean on the sweet side,

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:16.170
I'm gonna take some Greek yogurt

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:19.050
and spirulina and dye to
get that ocean blue color.

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:21.930
Last time, Jeremy got
eaten alive in the comments

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:23.430
for how much food dye he used.

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:25.800
So I'm trying to go the natural route,

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:26.910
so don't come for me.

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:30.240
So I'm just gonna put some
yogurt down here for our water.

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:32.100
Every morning we eat yogurt,

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:34.470
so I think this will draw him in.

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:36.600
And then once he tastes
everything, he'll love it.

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:38.520
This is his favorite
granola and I'm gonna put it

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:41.430
at the bottom, so it's like
the sandy bottom of the ocean.

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:43.980
I feel like I just wanna
make it a little more wavy.

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:46.920
Now we're gonna add our sailboat on top.

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:49.140
Now we gotta add all our sea creatures.

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:52.500
So we'll put a little
starfish, a little goldfish.

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:53.790
We got our sun.

00:06:53.790 --> 00:06:55.380
I think this is so cute.

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:56.790
I honestly am not the type of mom

00:06:56.790 --> 00:06:57.960
that does this type of stuff.

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:00.570
So when I do do it, it
makes me feel very happy

00:07:00.570 --> 00:07:02.430
and excited for his reaction.

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:06.030
Sailboat needs windows,
so with some banana slices

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:06.900
on there.

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:08.084
This is art.

00:07:08.084 --> 00:07:08.917
(Kelly laughing)

00:07:08.917 --> 00:07:10.560
I feel like I should
have maybe one more fish

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:12.240
and another starfish.

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:14.460
Okay, honestly, I feel pretty good.

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:16.650
I'm super excited to give this to Dylan.

00:07:16.650 --> 00:07:17.760
I think he's gonna love it.

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:19.770
I'm feeling really confident about this,

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:21.960
but Jeremy also is the breakfast king,

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:24.180
so I'm a little nervous to
see what he's come up with.

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:25.013
Let's go see.

00:07:25.013 --> 00:07:26.100
- Today for my meal,

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:28.110
I will be making a monster theme breakfast

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:30.120
because Dylan loves monsters

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:32.370
and I will be starting
with monster muffins.

00:07:32.370 --> 00:07:33.570
First of all, add our eggs.

00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:35.310
Dylan, when it comes to breakfast,

00:07:35.310 --> 00:07:37.980
is not a very picky eater,
but every other meal

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:38.937
throughout the day he is.

00:07:38.937 --> 00:07:40.980
And next we're gonna add our oats.

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:43.770
We're gonna add some
cinnamon, our flaxseed.

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:46.590
We're gonna add one
banana and some spinach

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:48.450
because these are healthy muffins today.

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:50.130
Dylan usually doesn't eat his veggies,

00:07:50.130 --> 00:07:51.480
so we try to find ways to sneak it

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:52.500
into whatever we're doing.

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:54.780
We're gonna add a little
green food coloring

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:56.370
just to brighten it up a little bit

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:57.720
and then blend everything together.

00:07:57.720 --> 00:07:58.553
It's looking pretty good.

00:07:58.553 --> 00:08:00.870
The color we want is there,
so as we're cooking it,

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:02.970
the color's gonna die down
a little bit in the oven.

00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:05.370
Now we're just gonna pour
it into our muffin tins

00:08:05.370 --> 00:08:06.510
and get ready to bake them.

00:08:06.510 --> 00:08:09.960
I have not made these muffins
before, but based on Dylan,

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:11.430
I think he is going to enjoy them.

00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:12.330
A little bit of a risk.

00:08:12.330 --> 00:08:14.163
I don't know, after the last competition,

00:08:14.163 --> 00:08:16.050
I got my butt kicked a little bit,

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:17.400
but we'll see what we can do.

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:18.510
So the last thing I'm gonna do is

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:20.460
add these little candy monster eyes

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:23.610
just to make them look a
little bit more like monsters.

00:08:23.610 --> 00:08:25.357
He's been telling me for weeks now,

00:08:25.357 --> 00:08:27.540
"I'm gonna pick you no
matter what the results are,"

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:29.640
so I'm feeling pretty confident today.

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:31.048
- [Katie] It's gonna
be a blind taste test.

00:08:31.048 --> 00:08:32.521
- I know, that's the one part

00:08:32.521 --> 00:08:34.048
I'm worried about is the blind taste test.

00:08:34.048 --> 00:08:37.020
And now we're gonna bake
these at 350 degrees

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:38.550
for about 20 minutes.

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:40.020
While the muffins are in the oven,

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:42.330
we're gonna move on to
our monster face paninis.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:44.790
So first, we're gonna crack our eggs.

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.650
I am the king of breakfast,

00:08:46.650 --> 00:08:48.840
which is why I normally don't need

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:50.280
to use these little tricks.

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:52.140
But today I'll do what I have to do.

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:54.570
So we're just gonna add a
little butter to our pan,

00:08:54.570 --> 00:08:57.000
whisk our eggs until
they're nice and light.

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:59.281
I do use a lot of butter in breakfast.

00:08:59.281 --> 00:09:00.720
It's the most important meal of the day.

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:02.610
Now the butter's nice and
melted, we're just gonna add

00:09:02.610 --> 00:09:06.000
in our eggs and keep them
moving to make them nice

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:07.080
and fluffy as they cook.

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:09.150
So I'm just making the egg into a square

00:09:09.150 --> 00:09:11.700
to make it fit nicely onto
the bread for our panini.

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:13.200
Just give it a nice little flip

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:14.800
and the eggs are ready for the panini.

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:17.310
We're just gonna take
our two pieces of bread

00:09:17.310 --> 00:09:18.866
and we're gonna start building our panini.

00:09:18.866 --> 00:09:19.920
So we're gonna add our egg.

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:22.080
Now, our egg's on the bread,
we're gonna add a few pieces

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:24.990
of bacon, already have some
cooked bacon ready to go.

00:09:24.990 --> 00:09:27.300
And then we're gonna top our bacon

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:29.250
with a little bit of cheddar cheese.

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:31.470
Dylan loves cheese, he is always looking

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:32.730
for the perfect cheese pull.

00:09:32.730 --> 00:09:34.200
Our sandwich is ready to go

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:36.870
and next step is we're gonna
grill it on the panini press.

00:09:36.870 --> 00:09:38.910
So first we're gonna spray our press.

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:40.830
And now we're gonna add our sandwich.

00:09:40.830 --> 00:09:42.420
We're gonna cook this
for about two minutes

00:09:42.420 --> 00:09:43.920
until it's golden brown and crispy.

00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:45.960
All right, now that our
sandwich is golden brown

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:48.300
and ready to go, we're gonna
take it off the panini press

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:49.920
and start building our monster face.

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:50.753
First thing we're gonna do

00:09:50.753 --> 00:09:53.280
for the monster face is cut out circles

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:55.050
of Canadian bacon for the eyes.

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:57.180
I don't think Dylan's ever
had Canadian bacon before,

00:09:57.180 --> 00:09:59.670
so it's another risk I'm gonna
take, but it's delicious,

00:09:59.670 --> 00:10:01.140
so can't go wrong with it.

00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:04.470
Now we're just gonna cut little
slices in our Canadian bacon

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:07.890
so we could pop the hard
boiled egg eyes through.

00:10:07.890 --> 00:10:10.170
Now, this is the part I'm
worried about the most

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:12.510
'cause I don't think Dylan
likes hard boiled eggs,

00:10:12.510 --> 00:10:14.220
but we are going to find out today.

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:15.300
The eyes look okay,

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:18.780
I think what gives eyes
expression is the eyebrows,

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:20.700
so once I add some angry
eyebrows onto there,

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:21.930
I think they'll look a little better.

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:24.270
I think the eyebrows give
them a little more expression.

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:26.790
Next, we are going to
cut a red bell pepper

00:10:26.790 --> 00:10:29.730
for the mouth and we're
just going to slice it

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:32.460
into little strips and
then make it nice and spiky

00:10:32.460 --> 00:10:33.390
so it looks like teeth.

00:10:33.390 --> 00:10:34.830
And now we have our little mouth.

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:36.780
Last thing I'm gonna do
is slice a few pieces

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:38.370
of kiwi just for the arms and legs

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:39.870
so it looks like a scary monster.

00:10:39.870 --> 00:10:40.703
What do you think?

00:10:40.703 --> 00:10:41.536
That's a scary sandwich.

00:10:41.536 --> 00:10:43.290
Now that we're finished with our panini,

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:45.060
we're gonna check back
in with our muffins.

00:10:45.060 --> 00:10:46.800
Now that our muffins are out of the oven,

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:49.170
we're going to fill them with Nutella

00:10:49.170 --> 00:10:50.970
just to give them a special little treat.

00:10:50.970 --> 00:10:52.350
Dylan does have a little sweet tooth,

00:10:52.350 --> 00:10:55.140
but normally not in actual meals.

00:10:55.140 --> 00:10:56.820
Now that our muffins are
done, we're gonna move on

00:10:56.820 --> 00:10:59.130
to our next step, which
is a fruit smoothie.

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:01.020
So first we're gonna
add some frozen peaches,

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:03.780
some frozen banana, frozen
chunks of pineapple,

00:11:03.780 --> 00:11:06.120
and two big handfuls of spinach.

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:09.120
Dylan will usually take about three sips

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:10.740
of my breakfast smoothie every morning.

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:13.230
So I know he'll like it,
especially with the green color,

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:14.940
green is his favorite color.

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:16.470
And now I'm just gonna add a little bit

00:11:16.470 --> 00:11:18.660
of coconut milk to blend it all together

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:19.620
and make a nice smoothie.

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:21.510
All right, now that our
smoothie is all blended

00:11:21.510 --> 00:11:23.280
and good to go, we are going to pour it

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:25.290
into our glass and get
our garnishes ready.

00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:29.250
I chose this smoothie because
every Sunday morning we go

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:31.200
to the farmer's market as a family.

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:34.350
The first stop at the farmer's
market is I get a green juice

00:11:34.350 --> 00:11:36.990
for myself and I might get two sips

00:11:36.990 --> 00:11:39.390
in before Dylan finishes
the rest of my green juice.

00:11:39.390 --> 00:11:40.950
Now that our smoothie is in our glass,

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:42.330
we are going to garnish it

00:11:42.330 --> 00:11:45.690
with little eyes made out
of bananas and blueberry.

00:11:45.690 --> 00:11:48.090
So we're just gonna poke a
little hole in the banana

00:11:48.090 --> 00:11:51.180
with a glass straw so we could
fit our blueberry in there.

00:11:51.180 --> 00:11:52.380
We have our little eyeball.

00:11:52.380 --> 00:11:54.570
Now that I have some skewers,
I cut them down to size

00:11:54.570 --> 00:11:56.280
and they'll fit perfectly in our glass.

00:11:56.280 --> 00:11:58.740
And there is our monster berry smoothie.

00:11:58.740 --> 00:12:00.090
I feel really good about this one.

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:01.440
I think this might be his favorite part

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:02.617
of the entire breakfast.

00:12:02.617 --> 00:12:04.200
So the last thing we're gonna make is

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:05.880
some fun fruit monsters.

00:12:05.880 --> 00:12:08.370
So we're just gonna make
a little monster mouth.

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:10.590
We're gonna cut our apple into slices.

00:12:10.590 --> 00:12:13.080
Next, we're gonna spread
a little almond butter

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:15.810
inside the apple, gonna
put these two together.

00:12:15.810 --> 00:12:18.960
And now we're just gonna put
in some yogurt-covered raisins

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:20.220
to look like little monster teeth.

00:12:20.220 --> 00:12:23.640
For the monster's eyes, we're
gonna put some marshmallows

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:26.760
on toothpicks with little
chocolate chips in the middle,

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:28.890
and that'll also help it hold
the whole thing together.

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:30.150
Now we have a monster mouth.

00:12:30.150 --> 00:12:32.160
Next, we are gonna make a monster kiwi.

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:34.320
It's mostly eyes and
teeth in making monsters.

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:36.120
There's not much of an art to it.

00:12:36.120 --> 00:12:38.940
It's just try to make it look
as fun and scary as you can.

00:12:38.940 --> 00:12:40.950
We're gonna do a few slices of kiwi.

00:12:40.950 --> 00:12:43.230
We're just gonna take
our first slice of kiwi.

00:12:43.230 --> 00:12:45.210
Put a little slice of strawberry

00:12:45.210 --> 00:12:46.620
in the middle to make a little tongue.

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:48.300
And now we're gonna take our toothpick.

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:51.720
We're gonna add our
marshmallows and chocolate chips

00:12:51.720 --> 00:12:53.550
to make our eyes for this little monster.

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:55.470
Toothpicks are pretty
dangerous around our kids,

00:12:55.470 --> 00:12:56.940
so you have to be a little careful

00:12:56.940 --> 00:12:58.890
when making monsters outta food.

00:12:58.890 --> 00:13:00.630
And now we have our kiwi monster.

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:03.480
For our last monster,
we're going to do orange

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:07.290
with some blueberry arms and
legs and a pineapple Mohawk.

00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:08.490
And he does love Mohawks.

00:13:08.490 --> 00:13:09.750
I'm just taking blueberries

00:13:09.750 --> 00:13:12.030
and putting them onto a toothpick

00:13:12.030 --> 00:13:13.710
and then putting the
toothpick into the orange.

00:13:13.710 --> 00:13:16.080
So now we have the body for our monster

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:18.690
and we're going to make
a little pineapple Mohawk

00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:19.770
and stick that in.

00:13:19.770 --> 00:13:21.330
And for the monster's eyeball,

00:13:21.330 --> 00:13:24.030
since it's not related to
the chocolate chip monsters,

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:26.130
we are going to use a raisin for the eye.

00:13:26.130 --> 00:13:27.780
Now that our monsters are assembled,

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:30.090
I'm gonna get everything
together and assemble our plate.

00:13:30.090 --> 00:13:32.790
So first thing we're gonna
do is move our sandwich over.

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:34.890
That's gonna be the
centerpiece of our plate

00:13:34.890 --> 00:13:37.410
with its little kiwi arms and legs.

00:13:37.410 --> 00:13:40.050
Next we're gonna add our scariest muffin.

00:13:40.050 --> 00:13:42.150
Now we're gonna put our
smoothie on the plate

00:13:42.150 --> 00:13:44.970
and I'm gonna try to stand up the cyclops.

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:47.130
Now we'll add our little fruit monsters

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:48.660
and breakfast is served.

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:50.850
It is a real monster party for breakfast.

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:51.683
I feel good.

00:13:51.683 --> 00:13:53.670
I think I do have a chance
at redemption today.

00:13:53.670 --> 00:13:55.410
Now let's go see what Dylan thinks.

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:57.147
Better not let me down.

00:13:57.147 --> 00:13:58.818
- [Woman] And open.

00:13:58.818 --> 00:13:59.651
(Dylan chuckling)

00:13:59.651 --> 00:14:00.484
(Kelly laughing)

00:14:00.484 --> 00:14:01.380
- Monsters?

00:14:01.380 --> 00:14:03.180
Green's my favorite color.

00:14:03.180 --> 00:14:04.613
I'm gonna try this first.

00:14:05.503 --> 00:14:06.336
I like it.

00:14:06.336 --> 00:14:08.703
The alien, I like Mohawks.

00:14:09.810 --> 00:14:11.373
I like the blueberries.

00:14:14.490 --> 00:14:16.380
I taste bacon and eggs.

00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:17.400
He looks funny.

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:19.083
I think it's chocolate inside.

00:14:20.580 --> 00:14:22.050
- [Katie] What's your
favorite thing you've eaten?

00:14:22.050 --> 00:14:23.256
- The blueberries.

00:14:23.256 --> 00:14:24.090
(Kelly laughing)

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:26.028
I like this for breakfast.

00:14:26.028 --> 00:14:27.817
Please bring in the next dish.

00:14:27.817 --> 00:14:29.568
- [Katie] All right, and open your eyes.

00:14:29.568 --> 00:14:30.962
- Wow!

00:14:30.962 --> 00:14:31.848
It's the beach.

00:14:31.848 --> 00:14:32.681
I like the other one,

00:14:32.681 --> 00:14:34.590
but I don't know what this tastes like.

00:14:35.857 --> 00:14:37.650
It tastes like candy.

00:14:37.650 --> 00:14:39.683
There's a boat on it.

00:14:39.683 --> 00:14:42.093
I don't really like the pancakes.

00:14:43.530 --> 00:14:44.850
I like the fish.

00:14:44.850 --> 00:14:46.410
Eggs!

00:14:46.410 --> 00:14:47.798
I like it.

00:14:47.798 --> 00:14:48.631
It's decision time!

00:14:48.631 --> 00:14:51.813
- Did you like the ocean
plate or the monster plate?

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:54.217
- Monster.

00:14:54.217 --> 00:14:55.242
(Kelly and Jeremy applauding)

00:14:55.242 --> 00:14:56.075
- Whoo!

00:14:56.075 --> 00:14:57.647
- Daddy won!

00:14:57.647 --> 00:14:58.618
- Good job, dad.

00:14:58.618 --> 00:14:59.451
- Thanks, dude.

00:14:59.451 --> 00:15:01.320
- Good job, Dylan, and great job, Jeremy.

00:15:01.320 --> 00:15:02.640
I guess we're tied now.

00:15:02.640 --> 00:15:04.940
Thanks so much for watching
and we'll see you next time.

00:15:04.940 --> 00:15:05.773
Bye!

00:15:05.773 --> 00:15:06.606
Say bye.

00:15:06.606 --> 00:15:08.040
- Bye!

00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:08.873
- [Man] Oh, yes!

00:15:10.949 --> 00:15:13.532
(upbeat music)

